{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":515096,"ns":0,"title":"Canonical form","extract":"In mathematics and computer science, a canonical, normal, or standard form of a mathematical object is a standard way of presenting that object as a mathematical expression. Often, it is one which provides the simplest representation of an object and allows it to be identified in a unique way.","description":"Standard representation of a mathematical object","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}